==English==

===Etymology===
Derived in English from {{suffix|en|psychosis|tic}}; compare {{cog|fr|psychotique}}, {{cog|de|psychotisch}}. Attested from the late 19th century. Compare earlier {{m|en|neurotic}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˌsaɪˈkɒtɪk/}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-psychotic.wav|a=Southern England}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# Of, related to, or suffering from [[psychosis]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1995| title=Forensic Neuropsychology|author=José A. Valciukas | page=277| passage=Direct evidence on '''psychotic''' behavior is the presence of either delusions or hallucinations (without insight into their pathological nature).}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2014|author=w:Ian McEwan|title=[[w:The Children Act (novel)|The Children Act]]|publisher=Penguin Random House (2018)|page=152|passage=She suffered '''psychotic''' episodes during which she believed herself to be spied upon by light bulbs.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2017| title=My Lovely Wife: A Memoir of Madness and Hope|author=Mark Lukach | page=| passage=She couldn't possibly know that I was parking in the same spot to visit my '''psychotic''' wife on the third floor of the hospital, the floor that needed a special elevator for access.}}
# {{lb|en|informal}} Out of control, [[bizarre]], or [[crazy]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2012| title=I Was a Killing Joke: A Bird's Eye View|author=Jodi.C.King | page=| passage=Full-bodied tribal rhythms, weird bendy bass lines, screechy high-end guitar melodies, and more '''psychotic''' lyrics about "Tension," "Butchers," and "Madness."}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2013| title=Youth and Internet Addiction in China|author=Trent Bax | page=| passage=This had left the mother feeling "'''psychotic'''" and "helpless" because she could not change the family, the school, and society that she said had all caused the son harm.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2017| title=A Game of Ghosts|author=John Connolly | page=14| passage=And if you ever try to record one of our conversations again, I'll set the dogs on you and your '''psychotic''' friends, and let them tear you all apart.}}

